releases.body:
1) Overview mode allows monitoring multiple terminals and visually switching between them:
- to enter Overview mode, swipe down from the tab bar (swipe up if the tab bar is at the bottom);
- to quickly switch to another terminal while entering the Overview screen, without lifting the finger, move over the desired terminal card and release;
- by default, the refresh rate of terminals in the Overview screen is limited to 5 FPS – adjustable or can be disabled in Settings on the Display screen under the Terminal section;
2) Sentence-level autocompletion in the input bar: sentences sent via the input bar are indexed and suggested while typing the next sentence (can be disabled in the Input Bar settings on the Input settings screen);
3) Added orientation-adaptive options to the settings for comfortable landscape mode use on smartphones: fullscreen mode, tab bar position, tab height, and showing the additional buttons bar;
4) Added an option to the long-press context menu in the terminal window to copy the selected terminal content as a single line;
5) Improvements to the input bar and autocompletion.

